#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1127 expect=skipped domain=DO
#note "Pins the wave-15 `Domains.Exclude: [DO]` entry — the translation of the `(-DO)` carve-out in this rule's own sheet scope string `CO, INTERVENTIONS, FINDINGS (-DO), EVENTS, FINDINGS ABOUT`, which wave 13 left untranslated and wave 14 translated on `PMDA-SD1125` only. ⚑ The neuter-and-watch is UNMASKED and the fixture is deliberately built so ONLY the new Exclude entry can reject it: the class is declared FINDINGS (so `Classes.Include` is satisfied), `DO` is none of the pre-existing `DM`/`SE`/`SM`/`SV` entries, all four required columns exist, and `DOTPTNUM` genuinely differs across two rows sharing `DOTPT=Baseline`, `DOTPTREF=REF1`, `VISITNUM=1`. Remove `DO` from the Exclude list and this scenario turns from `skipped` into a violation."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset DO class=FINDINGS label="Device Properties"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
col DOTPTNUM type=Num  label="Planned Time Point Number"
col DOTPTREF type=Char label="Time Point Reference"
col DOTPT    type=Char label="Planned Time Point Name"
---
S1 | DO | 001 | 1 | 1 | REF1 | Baseline
S1 | DO | 001 | 1 | 2 | REF1 | Baseline
---
